= The Left SRs Are Expelled

In the second half of November the SR party's Central Committee, meeting after its congress, expelled the Left SRs for forming a separate organisation. The Left SRs have called a founding congress for early December: 116 delegates from 99 organisations. [? if bol_regime = 1 : They will take seven seats in Lenin's government before the month is out. ?]

The left wing is a fifth of the party's members, and nearly all of its voters in the Baltic Fleet, in the Petrograd garrison and in many a village.

- @found: Hold the founding congress in December.
- @reconcile: Seek reconciliation, and stay in the party.

@found
on-arrival: {!
Q.lsr_split = 1;
RO.add(Q, {rel_ally: -8});
RO.boost(Q, {peasants: 2, soldiers: 2});
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 2, -2);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, -3);
!}

The founding congress of the Party of Left Socialist Revolutionaries met in Petrograd on 2 December, with 116 delegates from 99 organisations. It elected Spiridonova, Kamkov and Natanson, and proclaimed that the party would defend the peasants' land and the soviets.

@reconcile
choose-if: rel_ally >= 55
unavailable-subtitle: The SR leaders will not take the Left SRs back.
on-arrival: {!
Q.lsr_kept = 1;
RO.add(Q, {rel_ally: 6});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, 12);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 3, -4);
RO.boost(Q, {peasants: -2});
!}

The Left SRs have asked the Central Committee to withdraw the expulsion, and have been given a pledge on the Assembly and the land. The party is whole, and the left has the satisfaction of having been asked to stay.
